# Cursor Rules for CV and Motivation Letter Generation

**Ecosystem naming:** The public name of the music metadata ecosystem is **TheMusicTree**. **Primary link (portfolio):** `https://themusictree.org`. Open-source repositories are under the GitHub organization **BehindTheMusicTree**—use **TheMusicTree** in narrative copy (CV, motivation letters); when a single URL is needed for the venture, prefer the portfolio; add `https://github.com/BehindTheMusicTree` when code or the org is the point.

**TheMusicTree frontends (Vercel):** User-facing **Next.js** apps are deployed on **Vercel**, including the portfolio (**themusictree.org**), **GrowTheMusicTree** (**grow.themusictree.org**), and **AudioMeta Webapp** (**audiometa.themusictree.org**). Mention **Vercel** when describing these products or the frontend stack—not for backend-only services (e.g. Django APIs, Flask microservices) unless the copy is explicitly about those apps.

**Git branching terminology:** Write **GitFlow** as one word (camelCase). Do **not** write "Git Flow" (two words). If the lighter GitHub-centric workflow is meant, use **GitHub Flow**, not "Light Git Flow" or "git flow".

## CV and Motivation Letter Generation Process

When the user asks to generate a CV and/or motivation letter for a job application:

1. **Locate the job folder**: Each posting has a **dedicated directory** under `professional/CV/Jobs/[job title]/`. The job description is typically `Job Description.md` in that folder (alternatively `Description.txt` if already present). If the user gives a path or job title, use that folder under `Jobs/`.

2. **Read required files**:

   - Read the job description from the located path (typically `Job Description.md`)
   - Read `professional/CV/cv_format_spec.md` to understand the format requirements
   - Read `README.md` from the repository root as the source of truth for all experiences, projects, achievements, and skills

3. **Generate cv.md**:

   - Create `professional/CV/Jobs/[job title]/cv.md` in the same directory as the job description
   - **Do not name the employer, their products, programmes, brands, or internal project names** as they appear in the job description (e.g. recruiter company, product codename, programme label). The CV must stay **portable**: align skills and experience with the JD **without** echoing those names. Optional **Open to** line stays generic (sectors, stacks), not “poste chez X”. **motivation_letter.md** may name the employer and role (cover letter context).
   - Follow the format specified in `professional/CV/cv_format_spec.md`:
     - **Intro Section**: Opening line with title/role tags, 2 paragraphs about professional identity, optional key achievements. Must be between 570 and 580 characters in length (excluding project links in parentheses). **Best practice:** Write both paragraphs as **full, narrative sentences** with clear subject and verb (e.g. "Je construis…", "J'ai travaillé…"). Do **not** use a telegram-style or list-like second paragraph (e.g. chaining noun phrases or fragments separated only by periods: "APIs REST et modèles. Projet A. Expérience X. Langues."). Prefer 1–2 complete sentences per paragraph that tell a short narrative (what you build, with what, what it shows). Use real, flowing sentences, not fragmented bullet-style text.
     - **Skills Section**: Technical skills (Techniques) and project/process skills (Workflow) relevant to the job description, selected from README.md. Format: "Techniques: [comma-separated list]" and "Workflow: [comma-separated list]". Maximum 9 keywords for Techniques and maximum 9 keywords for Workflow. The language should match the job description language.
     - **Job Experiences Section**: Maximum 3 job experiences selected from README.md "Professional Experience" section **based on relevance to the job description**. **Experiences must always be listed in reverse chronological order (most recent first)**. Each with:
       - `[ICON]` Company/Project Name - Role Title (use `[ICON]` placeholder instead of markdown links)
       - Date Range (e.g., "Dec. 2021 – Present")
       - 2-3 bullet points written as plain text sentences without bullet markers (no "-" prefix). Each bullet point must be a complete, real sentence (not fragmented bullet-style text). Bullet points should start with past participles (e.g., "Développé", "Créé", "Implémenté") rather than using "Je" or "J'ai". Each bullet point should be approximately 95 characters in length (excluding project links in parentheses).
       - When mentioning specific projects, include project link(s) in parentheses immediately after the project name: `ProjectName (https://url.com)`. Priority order for links: website > PyPI > GitHub. **Available links (first priority, mention systematically they are wip where applicable):** AudioMeta Webapp: https://themusictree.org/projects/audiometa-webapp or https://audiometa.themusictree.org/ (Next.js on **Vercel**) ; GrowTheMusicTree: https://grow.themusictree.org/ (Next.js on **Vercel**) ; portfolio: https://themusictree.org/ (Next.js on **Vercel**) ; HearTheMusicTree: https://hear-api.themusictree.org/docs/ . Only one link per project in intro section.
     - **Links Section**: After the job experiences section, include a "Links" subsection listing all URLs in the format: `Project/Company Name: https://url.com`
     - **More Info Section**: Technical stack (grouped by Backend/Frontend/Database/DevOps), Education, Languages, Open to opportunities

4. **Generate motivation_letter.md**:

   - Create `professional/CV/Jobs/[job title]/motivation_letter.md` in the same directory as the job description
   - Follow a concise 2-3 paragraph structure:
     - **Paragraph 1**: Opening & Interest - express genuine interest, mention discovery, align with career goals
     - **Paragraph 2**: Relevant Experience & Skills - reference 2-3 key requirements from job description, connect to README experiences, highlight matching technical skills, include metrics
     - **Paragraph 3 (optional)**: Cultural Fit & Closing - briefly reference alignment with company values, express willingness to discuss, professional closing
   - Must be tailored to the specific job description
   - Must reference specific requirements from the job description
   - Must connect experiences from README.md to job requirements
   - Length: 2-3 paragraphs maximum, very concise and focused (significantly shorter than previous versions)
   - Tone: Professional, enthusiastic, authentic

5. **Validation step** - After generating cv.md:

   - **Run the validation script**: Execute `python3 professional/CV/validate_cv.py professional/CV/Jobs/[job title]/cv.md` to validate the CV format
   - The script checks:
     - Intro section is between 570 and 580 characters in length (excluding project links in parentheses)
     - All bullet points in the job experiences section are approximately 95 characters in length (excluding project links in parentheses, target range: 85-105 characters)
   - If validation fails, adjust any bullet points or intro section that do not meet these requirements
   - Continue adjusting until the validation script passes

6. **Key principles**:

   - **CV vs job description names**: In **cv.md** only, never cite names taken from the posting (company, product, ministry programme, incubator label, etc.); express fit through **domains**, **stacks**, and **outcomes** instead. **motivation_letter.md** is where naming the organisation and mission is appropriate.
   - **TheMusicTree ecosystem**: Use **TheMusicTree** as the ecosystem/venture name in generated CV and motivation letter text (not “BehindTheMusicTree”). Job experience line format: `[ICON] TheMusicTree - Founder & Lead Developer` (or equivalent in the job description language). In the Links section, list the portfolio first: `TheMusicTree: https://themusictree.org`; include `https://github.com/BehindTheMusicTree` when the org or code is relevant.
   - **Bold important words**: In cv.md only, make important words **bold** (e.g. key skills, technologies, role titles, and achievements that match the job description). Do not use bold in motivation_letter.md.
   - All content must be based on information from README.md
   - Job experiences must be selected from README.md "Professional Experience" section (max 3) **based on relevance to the job description requirements**
   - Job experiences must always be listed in reverse chronological order (most recent first)
   - Always include metrics/quantifiable results when available
   - Use `[ICON]` placeholder instead of markdown links in the text
   - List all links separately after the relevant section in the format: `Project/Company Name: https://url.com`
   - Tailor content to match job description requirements
   - Use professional, authentic language
   - Avoid overusing the words "expert" or "expertise". Use alternative phrasing such as "experienced in", "skilled in", "proficient with", or describe specific achievements and capabilities instead.
   - **Phrasing for job experience bullet points**: Write complete, natural sentences that start with past participles (e.g., "Développé", "Créé", "Implémenté", "Contribué", "Collaboré"). Do not use "Je" or "J'ai" at the beginning of bullet points. Ensure sentences are real, flowing formulations, not fragmented bullet-style text.
   - The output language (for both cv.md and motivation_letter.md) must match the language of the job description. If the job description is in French, output in French. If in English, output in English.

7. **Output**: Put `Job Description.md`, `cv.md`, and `motivation_letter.md` together in `professional/CV/Jobs/[job title]/` (one subdirectory per posting).
